This project implements a Java-based text line detection system for bitmap images using graph algorithms. The goal is to identify and separate lines of text in an image without relying on machine learning or large labeled datasets.

The program converts an image into a weighted graph representation, where each pixel acts as a vertex and connections between pixels form weighted edges. Using Dijkstra’s shortest path algorithm, the program finds low-cost paths that correspond to whitespace between lines of text. These paths are used to determine the rows and columns that separate text, allowing the image to be processed into individual text regions.